<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><strong>CubeRush 3D</strong></p>
<p>Effective Date: November 13, 2026</p>

<section>
<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>Welcome to CubeRush 3D. Your privacy is important to us.
This Privacy Policy explains how CubeRush 3D handles information
when you use our Android application.</p>
<p>By using the application, you acknowledge this Privacy Policy.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>CubeRush 3D is designed to work without requiring users
to create an account or provide personal information.</p>
<p>The application stores certain gameplay information locally
on your device, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>Solving history and solve times.</li>
<li>Personal records and statistics.</li>
<li>XP, levels and achievements.</li>
<li>Completed lessons and challenges.</li>
<li>Application preferences and customization settings.</li>
</ul>
<p>This information is stored using local application storage
and is used to provide the app's features.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>3. Camera Permission</h2>
<p>CubeRush 3D may request access to your device camera
when you use the cube scanning feature.</p>
<p>The camera is used to detect and recognize the colors
of your physical Rubik's Cube.</p>
<p>Camera frames are processed within the application
for cube color detection. The scanner implementation
does not intentionally upload or store captured camera
frames on a remote server.</p>
<p>You can deny camera permission, although the camera
scanning feature will not work without it.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>4. Device Permissions</h2>
<p>The application may use the following permissions:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Camera:</strong> To scan Rubik's Cube colors.</li>
<li><strong>Vibration:</strong> To provide optional haptic feedback.</li>
<li><strong>Internet:</strong> Declared in the Android application
for supported platform functionality. This permission alone
does not mean personal information is collected.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section>
<h2>5. Data Storage and Security</h2>
<p>Gameplay records, statistics and settings are stored
locally on your device.</p>
<p>We do not operate a user account or cloud synchronization
service in the current application implementation.</p>
<p>Uninstalling the application or clearing its storage
may permanently remove locally saved gameplay information.</p>
<p>We take reasonable steps to protect information through
the security features provided by the Android platform.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>The current application implementation is designed
to provide its core gameplay features without requiring
third-party account services.</p>
<p>Google Play and Android may independently process
information according to their own privacy policies.</p>
<p>If third-party analytics, advertising or other data-processing
services are added in future versions, this policy will be
updated to describe their use.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>CubeRush 3D does not require users to submit personal
information to use its core features.</p>
<p>We do not knowingly collect personal information
directly from children through the application.</p>
<p>Parents or guardians who have privacy concerns may
contact us using the email address below.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>8. Your Privacy Choices</h2>
<p>You may:</p>
<ul>
<li>Deny camera permission through Android settings.</li>
<li>Clear locally stored application data through Android settings.</li>
<li>Uninstall the application to remove its local application data.</li>
<li>Contact us with privacy-related questions or requests.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section>
<h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy when application
features or data practices change.</p>
<p>Any updated version will be published at the official
Privacy Policy URL.</p>
</section>

